				\begin{document}$${\it\text{G}} = {\text{K}}{\lambda}/{\text{Dcos }}({\text{q}})$$\end{document}where the wavelength is λ, the Scherrer constant is K = 0.9, and the full width (in radians) of the peak intensity at half maximum is D, symbolic as (FWHM). The value of G was confirmed by using the U-fit program.

The beam diameter at the sample reached 5 cm. The power density, in this case, could be calculated as44:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
